class.description:
Every step only creates what is missing, so running it again changes nothing:
- the folders [code]res://jrpg[/code], [code]res://jrpg/db[/code] and [code]res://jrpg/maps[/code];
- the database manifest [code]res://jrpg/database.tres[/code] with one file per table plus System, types and terms in [code]res://jrpg/db[/code], filled with a few original starter entries (a hero and a class, Attack and Guard, a healing item, a weapon and an armor, an enemy and a troop, the Knocked Out and Guarding states). A table missing from an existing manifest is added; existing tables are never changed;
- a System game id when it is empty;
- the [code]jrpg_*[/code] input actions with keyboard and gamepad bindings; actions that already exist keep the user's mapping;
- the [code]jrpg/enabled[/code] project setting, which shows the JRPG workspace;
- the managed addon (see [JRPGManagedAddon]).
Editor only. The Claude bridge exposes it as the [code]jrpg_setup_project[/code] tool.
